COMMENT     PROVISIONAL REFSEQ: This record has not yet been subject to final
            NCBI review. The reference sequence is identical to K02121.
            The HRV-14 virion contains a ss-RNA genome that serves as a
            monocistronic mRNA for the synthesis of all viral structural and
            non-structural proteins.  The genome is polyadenylated on the 3'
            end and may be capped with a protein (VPg) on the 5' end (by
            analogy with other picornaviruses).
            Based on homology, HRV14 appears most closely related to poliovirus
            type 1 (PV-1); on these grounds, both [1] and [2] tentatively
            predict a number of mature products resulting from cleavage of the
            polyprotein precursor. The only major differences in these
            identifications concern the VP3 and VP1 coding sequences, about
            which [1] is uncertain.
            The sequence differences annotated as conflicts herein may in fact
            be natural variations.
            COMPLETENESS: full length.
